-- title:
--   Uniform geometric decay of Walsh norms for finite-rank operators
-- statement:
--   These notions belong to a proof that a real Banach space $X$ with the approximation property is K-convex (the Rademacher projection is bounded on $L_2(\{\pm1\}^n;X)$ uniformly in $n$) if and only if $X$ and its dual $X^*$ both have finite cotype. The converse direction shows that such $X$ has nontrivial type, i.e. does not contain $\ell_1^n$ uniformly, and then derives K-convexity from a power-gap estimate for commuting coordinate projections. A normed space $Z$ satisfies the fixed cotype bound of length $m$ with constant $D$ if $\bigl(\sum_{i\le m}\|z_i\|^2\bigr)^{1/2}\le D\bigl(\mathbb E\|\sum_{i\le m}\varepsilon_iz_i\|^2\bigr)^{1/2}$ for all $z_1,\dots,z_m\in Z$. Let $d(m)=\lceil2\log_2m\rceil$, and let $D_g,D_f\ge1$ satisfy $4\le d(m)<m$ and $80\,d(m)(d(m)+1)^2\le\min\bigl(\sqrt m/(48D_g),\sqrt m/(48D_f)\bigr)$. There is $n_0>4m$ such that $\rho(N)=(1/2)^{\lfloor(N-n_0)/(2m)\rfloor}\to0$ and the following holds. Let $X$ be a real Banach space with $X^*$ satisfying the fixed cotype bound of length $m$ with constant $D_g$, and $Y$ one with constant $D_f$. For every finite-rank operator $T:X\to Y$, $\omega_n(T)\le\frac12\omega_{n-2m}(T)$ for all $n\ge n_0$, and
--   $$
--   \omega_N(T)\le\rho(N)\,\|T\|\qquad\text{for all }N .
--   $$
--
--   The decay rate is uniform over all finite-rank operators between such spaces.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/Analysis/Cotype/UniformDecay.lean#L49-L97

